matmul.cpp, 2026-11-23

Benchmark results

Measured on arm64 macOS 26.6.2 with Apple Clang 17.0.0.
Built with clang++ -std=c++17 -O3 matmul.cpp -o matmul.
Each pass uses one warm-up and five timed calls per configuration.
Mean ms averages the two pass means. GFLOP/s uses 2 × M × K × N
divided by the mean runtime and converted to billions of FLOPs per second.
Timing includes output allocation and initialization. Input generation and
correctness checks run outside the timed region.

Loop order refers to the outer tile loops for tiled kernels. Both tiled
kernels use i-k-j inside each tile. i is row, j is column, and k is the
shared dimension.
A-tile reuse keeps A's (i, k) tile fixed while visiting column tiles j.
Output-tile accumulation completes C's (i, j) tile across all k tiles.

512 × 512

