Large-matrix blocking experiment

Measured with the existing kernels on arm64 using Apple Clang 17.0.0
with -std=c++17 -O3. B occupied 16 MiB at 2048 and 64 MiB at 4096.
Each size began with an untimed reordered run that warmed up the kernel
and produced the reference. Nine reference entries were verified using
double-precision dot products. Each timed result was compared against the
full reference outside the timed region. Timing includes output allocation
and initialization. GFLOP/s counts 2 × M × K × N FLOPs.

Each configuration was timed once during the sweep. Block sizes increased
from 32 to a full-size tile in powers of two. The reordered baseline and
the two finalists were then timed twice more, with the order reversed for
the second confirmation run. At 2048 the finalists were the fastest tiled
configurations, including the full-size control. At 4096 the finalists were
the fastest multi-tile configurations, with full-size tiles as controls.

