Four-row B reuse (matmul_multirow)

Measured the current kernel on arm64 with Apple Clang 17.0.0 and
-std=c++17 -O3. Each kernel used the existing benchmark helper with one
warm-up and five timed calls on the same inputs. All row counts were
divisible by four. Reordered was timed again for this comparison.

Correctness was checked against the naive kernel at 512 and 1024, and
against reordered at 2048 and 4096. Nine entries of each reference were
verified with double-precision dot products. Input generation and
correctness checks ran outside the timed region. Speedup is reordered
mean runtime divided by multirow mean runtime.

